  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "$$\n{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ -3{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-2{e}^{t} \\\\ 6{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in R\n$$\n\nConsider the vector-valued functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ above. Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are solutions of the same system of linear ODEs, select the correct options in the reasoning below.$\\,$ The Wronskian is $W({x}_{1},{x}_{2})=$ \n{{field-1}},\nwhich is\n{{field-2}}.  \n\n$\\,$ Therefore, the set ${{x}_{1}(t),{x}_{2}(t)}$ is linearly \n{{field-3}} \non $R.$",
